=== HINT 1 ===
GetModuleHandleA(NULL) returns the HMODULE (base VA) of the calling process.
Cast it directly to PIMAGE_DOS_HEADER.

=== HINT 2 ===
IMAGE_DOS_HEADER.e_lfanew is a LONG offset from the base to the NT headers.
  PIMAGE_NT_HEADERS nt = (PIMAGE_NT_HEADERS)((BYTE*)base + dos->e_lfanew);

Magic values:
  IMAGE_DOS_SIGNATURE  = 0x5A4D  ("MZ")
  IMAGE_NT_SIGNATURE   = 0x00004550  ("PE\0\0")

Fields to print:
  nt->OptionalHeader.ImageBase
  nt->OptionalHeader.AddressOfEntryPoint
  nt->FileHeader.NumberOfSections

=== HINT 3 (SPOILER) ===
HMODULE base = GetModuleHandleA(NULL);
PIMAGE_DOS_HEADER dos = (PIMAGE_DOS_HEADER)base;
if (dos->e_magic != IMAGE_DOS_SIGNATURE) { puts("Not a PE!"); return 1; }
PIMAGE_NT_HEADERS nt = (PIMAGE_NT_HEADERS)((BYTE*)base + dos->e_lfanew);
if (nt->Signature != IMAGE_NT_SIGNATURE) { puts("Bad NT sig!"); return 1; }
printf("ImageBase:          0x%llX\n", (unsigned long long)nt->OptionalHeader.ImageBase);
printf("EntryPoint RVA:     0x%lX\n",  nt->OptionalHeader.AddressOfEntryPoint);
printf("NumberOfSections:   %u\n",     nt->FileHeader.NumberOfSections);
